/* [REQUIRED HEADER NOTE, ASCII transliteration of the Chinese spec text -- KeYmaera X
 *  parses ASCII only]:
 *  This certificate proves the ALGEBRAIC EQUIVALENT of "assuming the perturbation
 *  magnitude delta_U1 is bounded, the Schur term at -b is O(b) and the eigenvalue
 *  correction is O(b^2)".  The concrete value delta_U1 = (-A^{-2} c)[0] is verified
 *  by verify_freq_mode.py (sympy), NOT here.
 *
 * dL is not an analysis package; the literal O(b^2) asymptotic is out of QE's reach.
 * The dL-provable equivalent below reduces the numerical O(b^2) fact to an algebra
 * identity.  Setup (Conventions sec.13.6, thmB_schur_vanishes):
 *   At mu=0:   (e1^T A^{-1} c) = U1_at_0,  with row-7 reading (-3/2 Vg) U1_at_0 = c6,
 *              and c6 = 0  =>  U1_at_0 = 0.
 *   At mu=-b:  (e1^T (A-mu I)^{-1} c) shifts by b * delta_U1, where delta_U1 stands
 *              for (-A^{-2} c)[0] (the first-order term in mu); so
 *              U1_at_negb = U1_at_0 + b * delta_U1.
 *   Schur term at -b:  rhoTu_at_negb = (-3/2 kappa Vg) * U1_at_negb.
 * Claim: rhoTu_at_negb = (-3/2 kappa Vg) * b * delta_U1, i.e. the Schur term at -b is
 * b * (constant) * delta_U1 = O(b)  (since U1_at_0 = 0 by Power Lock). */

/* Identifiers carry no underscores (KeYmaera X parser):
 *   U1at0 = U1_at_0,  U1atnegb = U1_at_negb,  rhoTuatnegb = rhoTu_at_negb,
 *   dU1 = delta_U1. */
Problem
  \forall b \forall kappa \forall Vg \forall U1at0 \forall U1atnegb
  \forall c6 \forall rhoTuatnegb \forall dU1
  ( b > 0 & Vg > 0
    & (-3/2*Vg)*U1at0 = c6
    & c6 = 0
    & U1atnegb = U1at0 + b*dU1
    & rhoTuatnegb = (-3/2*kappa*Vg)*U1atnegb
    -> rhoTuatnegb = (-3/2*kappa*Vg)*b*dU1 )
End.

